{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"h":0.015835813695325718,"c":1,"x":0.84111035496309794,"t":"Reading","y":0.060082163096026764,"w":0.081337922414143948},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.10755813925891966,"c":1,"t":"E","x":0.084362139972751438,"w":0.016460905075073251},{"w":0.76748972574869789,"h":0.018992932862190726,"c":1,"t":"Let us apply both the terms 'means' and 'end' to marketing. The students have signed","y":0.10600706674213844,"x":0.12962962267029374},{"c":1,"x":0.1315930698420156,"h":0.021200085697241411,"y":0.12422167774919357,"t":"up for a course in order to learn how to market effectively. But to what end? There seem","w":0.78617518107096351},{"c":1,"w":0.7654320780436199,"h":0.01896211648857915,"t":"to be two main attitudes toward that question. One is that the answer is obvious: the","x":0.12962963991369547,"y":0.14534883759722794},{"c":1,"h":0.018912468136269567,"w":0.78600824991861995,"t":"purpose of marketing is to sell things and to make money. The other attitude is that the","y":0.16424418643360994,"x":0.13168723304987176},{"y":0.18139335329178818,"w":0.7717642720540363,"h":0.022126370801802131,"c":1,"t":"purpose of marketing is irrelevant: Each person comes to the program and course with","x":0.12953448822997199},{"t":"his or her own plans, and these need not even concern the acquisition of marketing","x":0.12962963093900698,"y":0.20200235565426483,"w":0.74897120157877595,"c":1,"h":0.018927876323075465},{"x":0.12956981529065445,"c":1,"t":"expertise as such. My proposal, which I believe would also be Kant's, is that neither of","h":0.020863731842580169,"w":0.77174718221028638,"y":0.22090137114995501},{"h":0.02142838342170128,"x":0.12953832773415683,"w":0.77180257161458332,"t":"these attitudes captures the significance of the end to the means for marketing. A field","c":1,"y":0.23967337988144755},{"h":0.022399080094515966,"c":1,"x":0.12949802167716673,"t":"of knowledge or a professional endeavor is defined by both the means and the end;","y":0.25753656336343411,"w":0.74510197957356772},{"t":"hence both deserve scrutiny. Students need to study both how to achieve X, and also","y":0.27906976782836868,"w":0.75514404296875015,"h":0.018927876323075354,"c":1,"x":0.12962962460325372},{"w":0.097136713663736968,"t":"what X is.","y":0.29895991593853721,"h":0.016001517135206811,"x":0.12953406129205311,"c":1},{"w":0.77572016398111976,"c":1,"x":0.084362140046477144,"h":0.020413894114140407,"t":"F It is at this point that 'Arson for Profit' becomes supremely relevant. That course is","y":0.3255813949624875},{"y":0.34435579781875791,"w":0.7841560872395833,"x":0.12950645218861287,"t":"presumably all about means: how to detect and prosecute criminal activity. It is therefore","h":0.021965986146241789,"c":1},{"y":0.36440224198124538,"c":1,"w":0.74294321695963539,"t":"assumed that the end is good in an ethical sense. When I ask fire science students to","h":0.021395841672647853,"x":0.12954966373127511},{"x":0.12962962797769517,"t":"articulate the end, or purpose, of their field, they eventually gencralize to something like,","y":0.38515901080656278,"h":0.018910756240323456,"w":0.78806584676106772,"c":1},{"y":0.40253239128889562,"x":0.12962963003727415,"c":1,"h":0.020432724969547067,"w":0.76337448120117191,"t":"The safety and welfare of society,' which seems right. As we have seen, someone could"},{"x":0.12962962799900224,"h":0.019140164899882239,"c":1,"t":"use the very same knowledge of means to achieve a much less noble end, such as personal","w":0.78806584676106783,"y":0.42285041177471894},{"t":"profit via destructive, dangerous, reckless activity. But we would not call that firefighting.","w":0.77572016398111987,"c":1,"y":0.44186046492037356,"x":0.12962963015595277,"h":0.020448133156352966},{"t":"We have a separate word for it: arson. Similarly, if you employed the 'principles of","h":0.022722817141259899,"y":0.46029931229472121,"w":0.7265521240234375,"c":1,"x":0.1295384732679804},{"h":0.020348837575025036,"t":"marketing' in an unprincipled way, you would not be doing marketing. We have another","x":0.1275720199745613,"w":0.77160491943359366,"c":1,"y":0.47965116240434791},{"h":0.01889534805351778,"c":1,"y":0.50000000038853076,"w":0.72427983601888024,"t":"term for it: fraud. Kant gives the example of a doctor and a poisoner, who use the","x":0.12757201603864302},{"t":"identical knowledge to achieve their divergent ends. We would say that one is practicing","x":0.12757202817306448,"h":0.018944996405827363,"c":1,"y":0.51884570068779201,"w":0.78395060221354174},{"h":0.018975812779438939,"t":"medicine, the other, murder.","x":0.12757201495036979,"y":0.53916372170289306,"w":0.25925926208496097,"c":1},{"t":"25","c":1,"x":0.89300411474204788,"w":0.026748971939086985,"y":0.93313953471166133,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"t":"leltsresources.org","x":0.39467204139292561,"w":0.20852355957031249,"y":0.96598926647572159,"c":1,"h":0.01820395327007529}]}